*)
METHOD runManual : CNM_ReturnTypes.SingleExecutionState
VAR_INPUT
	execute :BOOL;
	pause :BOOL;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="runReferencing" Id="{b78a68f8-5c8c-42ea-9bab-b1e5422467be}" FolderPath="NonMandatory\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
## short summary
This method contains instructions and sequences for the referencing mode.
This mode is intended for referencing a machine with relative components, e.g. axes without absoulute position encodeing, torque driven axes (e.g. a press), coupling of master/slave axes.
If the node should do nothing, return a 'SUCCESS'.
It should run until all devices are referenced or the mode is stopped immedtiately or a stop request is raised (THIS^.modeControl.stopRequest).
This method is called automatically by the operation mode handler.

**attention**: If this method returns the state 'ERROR', the operation mode handler automatically disables the whole machine!

legal notes
